   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><b><div style=\"display:inline!important\"><font size=\"6\">Poppr 1.1.2 released</font></div></b><br></div><b><div><b><br></b></div><font size=\"4\"><a href=\"https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.1.1.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.1.1.2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480982790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FatymhWaqzEl2yVQtNqfp\">Here is a link to all the details</a></font></b><div><b><br></b></div><div>This release incorporates all of the functionalities that have been added in the development version including:</div><div><br></div><div><ul><li><span style=\"line-height:normal\">bootstrapping of any genetic distance</span></li><li><span style=\"line-height:normal\">handling polyploid data</span></li><li><span style=\"line-height:normal\">easier manipulation of hierarchical population structures with the genclone object</span></li><li><span style=\"line-height:normal\">an easy method for AMOVA</span></li></ul><div>Again, you can find out all of what has been added in the <b><a href=\"https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.1.1.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.1.1.2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480982790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FatymhWaqzEl2yVQtNqfp\">release notes</a></b><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>It is also important to point out that the vignette has been greatly shortened so as to only include data manipulation. For examples of analyses, you can visit <a href=\"http://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480982790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1GT9HCKiG0vENQMjqXK7dj\">a primer that was written by myself, Sydney E. Everhart, and Niklaus J. Grünwald here</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>All of this can be installed from CRAN using the function</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">install</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;poppr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font></div></code></div><br>If poppr has not been built for your system yet, you can use:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">install</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;poppr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;source&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font></div></code></div><br>if you have a C compiler (on Mac that would be bundled with the free XCode app). </div><div><br></div><div>Once you have poppr installed, you can type </div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#660\">?</span><span style=\"color:#000\">poppr</span></font></div></code></div><div>To see what&#39;s new.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Zhian</div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
